{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent positive bias: model forecasts are generally above realized prices, especially from ~day 10 onward. Apply a downward level shift (larger for longer horizons).",
    "Insufficient downside momentum: during selloffs the model declines too slowly and bottoms too high. Increase sensitivity to recent negative returns (steepen the downward slope) in the first 1–3 weeks.",
    "Overshoot on rebounds: after short-term upticks, the model projects a stronger/longer rebound than realized. Damp positive follow-through after a drawdown (cap rebound amplitude).",
    "Horizon-dependent error: near-term (days 1–5) errors are small; mid/long horizon (days 10–30) errors widen materially. Use horizon-weighted correction (minimal early, stronger later).",
    "Mean-reversion miscalibration: model reverts toward a higher mean than the market in these regimes. Re-anchor the long-run mean lower when the last 30d trend is negative."
  ]
}
